.TH NIVYX 1 "" "Nivyx" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
nivyx \- control the Nivyx system-wide DPI bypass service
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B nivyx
.I command
[options]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Nivyx runs as a system service that bypasses DPI-based blocking of HTTPS for
all applications and answers DNS over HTTPS. The
.B nivyx
command is its only public interface; everything below works the same on
Linux, macOS and Windows.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B status [--verbose]
Short summary: version, service, protection, DNS, mode.
.TP
.B doctor
Read-only health checks. Exit status 1 if a check failed.
.TP
.B diagnose \fIDOMAIN\fR [--verbose]
Explain DNS, HTTPS and the stored decision for one site.
.TP
.B stats
Local counters. No host names are shown or stored.
.TP
.B logs [\fIN\fR]
Recent log lines.
.TP
.B start | stop | restart | reload
Control the service (root). Stopping restores normal networking.
.TP
.B repair
Fix Nivyx-owned state only (root). Every repair is printed.
.TP
.B update [--check]
Check for, or install, the latest official release. The download is verified
against SHA256SUMS; a failed health check restores the previous version.
.TP
.B config show | path | check | set \fIDOMAIN STRATEGY\fR | unset \fIDOMAIN\fR
Inspect or change manual rules. Manual rules override automatic learning.
.TP
.B strategy \fIDOMAIN\fR
Which rule applies to a domain right now.
.TP
.B support-bundle [\fIFILE\fR]
Write a redacted diagnostics archive locally. Nothing is sent anywhere.
.TP
.B version
Print the version.
.TP
.B help [\fICOMMAND\fR]
Show help.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /etc/dpi-proxy/strategy.conf
Manual rules (Linux). macOS: /usr/local/etc/dpi-proxy/strategy.conf.
.SH SEE ALSO
https://github.com/kadireren7/nivyx
